=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
Full diagnostic sweep of the Kath4 topology finds no fault. Every OSPF adjacency across the Campus 1 / Campus 2 path is in Full state: mswitch0 peers with router16 (bond0 ↔ eth2), router16 peers with both mswitch0 and router7, router7 holds four Full neighbours (router1, router10, router8, router16), router17 holds four Full neighbours, and sshswitch peers with router17. Routing tables on all devices carry correct OSPF-learned paths in both directions — mswitch0 and router16 hold 10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24 via router7; sshswitch and router17 hold 172.16.10/20/30.0/24 via the same core. Live ping tests from three separate Campus 1 VLANs (PC5 on VLAN 10, PC9/PC11 on VLAN 20, PC14 on VLAN 30) to four Campus 2 hosts (PC1 at 10.5.0.1, PC3 at 10.6.0.3, PC4 at 10.6.0.4, dc_pc5 at 10.5.0.5) all returned 0% packet loss with TTL=58, consistent with correct 4-hop inter-campus routing. Router16's bond interface (eth0+eth1 bonded toward mswitch0) is UP and stable. The OSPF "death" the helpdesk references was either a transient flap that has since fully reconverged on its own, or the ticket was filed in error. No corrective action is required at this time; the network is healthy. Recommend monitoring router16's OSPF uptime over the coming days and configuring OSPF dead-interval/hello tuning or BFD on the router16 ↔ router7 link if flaps recur.
=== END ===